dartssh2  —  patches/dartssh2/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:  https://github.com/TerminalStudio/dartssh2
Version:   2.17.0
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) 2022 xuty

This is a MODIFIED fork, applied through `dependency_overrides` in pubspec.yaml.

Modifications: see git history under patches/dartssh2/. Diffed against the
unmodified pub.dev 2.17.0 release, the fork adds three things: (1)
chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com cipher support — a full AEAD encode/decode path
in ssh_transport.dart that upstream 2.17.0 never implemented; (2) zlib /
zlib@openssh.com compression negotiation and (de)compression, offered via a
new caller-controlled `algorithms.compress` list; (3) the SSH channel's
initial window bumped from 2 MiB to 16 MiB for high-BDP links. AES-GCM is NOT
part of this fork's changes — upstream 2.17.0's own default cipher list never
included GCM either way. AES-GCM is disabled one layer up, in the
application's own algorithm preference list (lib/ssh/ssh_connection.dart; see
commit 34c99e72): dartssh2 2.17's GCM support caused SSHAuthAbortError on
reconnect, so the app prefers chacha20-poly1305 first, then CTR, then CBC.

Full license text: patches/dartssh2/LICENSE

